question.text:
Consider two sets of $28$ paired observations $x_{1}, x_2, \ldots, x_{28},$ and $ y_{1}, y_2, \ldots, y_{28}.$ You are given that
\begin{align*}
&\sum_{i=1}^{28} x_i = 560, \qquad \sum_{i=1}^{28} y_i = 588, \\[5pt] 
&\sum_{i=1}^{28} x_i^2 = 10\,920, \qquad \sum_{i=1}^{28} y_i^2 = 13\,220.
\end{align*}
Calculate the sum of the squared deviations from the mean for the points $y_i.$

